WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:02.840 --> 00:00:05.440
STETSON: #acking Arts is
a festival and hackathon

00:00:05.440 --> 00:00:09.370
exploring the intersection of
art, entertainment, technology,

00:00:09.370 --> 00:00:10.960
and entrepreneurship.

00:00:10.960 --> 00:00:13.590
HALLWACHS: I come from a company
called Little Sun, but also

00:00:13.590 --> 00:00:16.320
from a work of art that's called
Little Sun and a global project

00:00:16.320 --> 00:00:17.740
that we would call Little Sun.

00:00:17.740 --> 00:00:20.280
It's based on the simple
but astonishing fact

00:00:20.280 --> 00:00:21.810
that 1.6 billion
people in the world

00:00:21.810 --> 00:00:23.710
don't have access
to electricity.

00:00:23.710 --> 00:00:26.350
The sun goes in the
top here, and then you

00:00:26.350 --> 00:00:28.307
have the little lamp
that shines in the night.

00:00:28.307 --> 00:00:29.390
You can take it traveling.

00:00:29.390 --> 00:00:30.389
You can take it walking.

00:00:30.389 --> 00:00:31.570
You can take it everywhere.

00:00:31.570 --> 00:00:34.070
[MUSIC PLAYING]

00:00:37.310 --> 00:00:38.744
Some people adopt it as art.

00:00:38.744 --> 00:00:39.910
Some will take it as design.

00:00:39.910 --> 00:00:41.346
Some will just
take it as a lamp,

00:00:41.346 --> 00:00:43.595
and others will take it as
a symbol of positive access

00:00:43.595 --> 00:00:44.620
to energy.

00:00:44.620 --> 00:00:46.870
It's about emotions,
beauty, and participation.

00:00:46.870 --> 00:00:49.520
AZEEM: What parts of Africa have
you been already operating in?

00:00:49.520 --> 00:00:51.820
HALLWACHS: We're operating
in Ethiopia, Kenya, Uganda,

00:00:51.820 --> 00:00:54.154
Zimbabwe, Senegal,
and South Africa.

00:00:54.154 --> 00:00:55.820
LUNG: With a hackathon,
you get a chance

00:00:55.820 --> 00:00:58.450
to go to work in something,
change it, see it

00:00:58.450 --> 00:00:59.926
in a different way.

00:00:59.926 --> 00:01:01.918
[MUSIC PLAYING]

00:01:03.420 --> 00:01:04.550
AZEEM: Make it simple.

00:01:04.550 --> 00:01:05.910
Simplicity's crucial.

00:01:05.910 --> 00:01:08.170
The idea should be like
an elevator pitch, right?

00:01:08.170 --> 00:01:09.162
SPEAKER 1: Oh, wow.

00:01:09.162 --> 00:01:10.650
AZEEM: Whoa, look at that.

00:01:10.650 --> 00:01:13.050
SPEAKER 2: I like that Little
Drop-Little Sun connection

00:01:13.050 --> 00:01:13.550
there.

00:01:13.550 --> 00:01:14.660
There's really striking.

00:01:14.660 --> 00:01:16.480
LUNG: We pass water
through a tube that's

00:01:16.480 --> 00:01:19.514
exposed to the UV light,
and it basically cleans out

00:01:19.514 --> 00:01:20.937
all the bacteria in the water.

00:01:20.937 --> 00:01:23.270
AZEEM: You can see that water
is kind of going this way.

00:01:23.270 --> 00:01:26.340
So you have the two LEDs,
and you have the LED

00:01:26.340 --> 00:01:27.720
that kind of powers that.

00:01:27.720 --> 00:01:30.364
KOVACIC: What we're
proposing is a community

00:01:30.364 --> 00:01:32.120
that's centered around
a website that's

00:01:32.120 --> 00:01:34.892
going to help the people
who are involved in selling

00:01:34.892 --> 00:01:38.420
and distributing Little Sun to
do three things-- to explore,

00:01:38.420 --> 00:01:39.591
to connect, and to join.

00:01:39.591 --> 00:01:41.632
OSMUNDSEN: We ended up
having a pretty even split

00:01:41.632 --> 00:01:43.930
of entrepreneurs,
artists, and engineers.

00:01:43.930 --> 00:01:47.135
We started out with just totally
bouncing off ideas and going

00:01:47.135 --> 00:01:49.925
super divergent, and
then whittling it down,

00:01:49.925 --> 00:01:52.060
and now we're finally
getting into actually

00:01:52.060 --> 00:01:53.040
building a prototype.

00:01:53.040 --> 00:01:55.620
PRESENTER: But how amazing
have the last two days been?

00:01:55.620 --> 00:01:57.016
Are you guys having fun?

00:01:57.016 --> 00:01:57.516
[CHEERING]

00:01:57.516 --> 00:02:00.330
HALLWACHS: I'm really curious
to see the community-based idea.

00:02:00.330 --> 00:02:02.038
Because that could be
an interesting part

00:02:02.038 --> 00:02:02.761
of exactly this.

00:02:02.761 --> 00:02:04.510
The communication is
really a vital thing.

00:02:04.510 --> 00:02:05.170
TANG: Hi, everyone.

00:02:05.170 --> 00:02:05.940
My name's Chris.

00:02:05.940 --> 00:02:06.910
TROEIN: I'm Maria.

00:02:06.910 --> 00:02:09.250
TANG: And we are part
of Little Sun Community.

00:02:09.250 --> 00:02:12.550
This is a platform which
connects vendors to one another

00:02:12.550 --> 00:02:16.180
to allow them to explore,
connect, and also join

00:02:16.180 --> 00:02:16.940
a community.

00:02:16.940 --> 00:02:19.260
Have you made art
with Little Sun?

00:02:19.260 --> 00:02:21.830
Have you found a practical
use for Little Sun?

00:02:21.830 --> 00:02:24.770
Or have you found it a cool
way of making it your newest

00:02:24.770 --> 00:02:26.005
fashion accessory?

00:02:26.005 --> 00:02:28.637
SPEAKER 3: A lot of those people
in those very same communities

00:02:28.637 --> 00:02:29.470
need something else.

00:02:29.470 --> 00:02:32.100
They need clean drinking water.

00:02:32.100 --> 00:02:34.660
This is Little Drop.

00:02:34.660 --> 00:02:38.670
It's a solar-powered LED
water treatment device.

00:02:38.670 --> 00:02:43.645
The straw spools through some
germicidal UV LED light bulbs.

00:02:43.645 --> 00:02:46.550
What the Little Drop
provides, like Little Sun,

00:02:46.550 --> 00:02:48.466
is an emotional experience.

00:02:48.466 --> 00:02:50.080
HOWARD: So you
differentiate yourself

00:02:50.080 --> 00:02:52.881
from the ones that are on
the market by-- it's more

00:02:52.881 --> 00:02:54.765
of an emotional connection?

00:02:54.765 --> 00:02:57.708
SPEAKER 4: Have you ever
heard the light of the sun?

00:02:57.708 --> 00:02:59.070
[TONES PLAYING]

00:03:01.340 --> 00:03:03.384
So basically, we're
hearing the light.

00:03:03.384 --> 00:03:05.800
FELDMAN: Transforming that
into an audio device, something

00:03:05.800 --> 00:03:07.800
you just did, like
over the last 48 hours?

00:03:07.800 --> 00:03:09.750
SPEAKER 5: It's, like,
extremely simple,

00:03:09.750 --> 00:03:13.080
directly wiring a hook-up
to this headphone jack.

00:03:13.080 --> 00:03:15.640
STETSON: The thing I find really
impressive about hackathons

00:03:15.640 --> 00:03:17.650
is people really
kind of come in,

00:03:17.650 --> 00:03:19.660
and they're just--
they're so completely

00:03:19.660 --> 00:03:21.644
open to making totally
new connections

00:03:21.644 --> 00:03:23.810
and then spending a lot of
time working on something

00:03:23.810 --> 00:03:25.412
with someone who they just met.

00:03:25.412 --> 00:03:27.870
HALLWACHS: The prize goes to
the Little Sun Community team.

00:03:27.870 --> 00:03:29.070
[CHEERING AND APPLAUSE]

00:03:30.570 --> 00:03:32.670
PRESENTER: Thank you for coming.

00:03:32.670 --> 00:03:35.120
[MUSIC PLAYING]

